# Find The Needle, Russian.
#
# An empty msgstr is not a bug: it means the string falls back to its message
# id, which is the English source text. See docs/localization/PLAN.md.
#
# Russian has three plural forms, so every plural entry here carries three
# msgstr lines: [0] for 1, 21, 31 (but not 11), [1] for 2 to 4 (and 22 to 24,
# and so on), [2] for everything else, 5 to 20 included.
#
# The rule is close to the Polish one but not the same: Polish counts 21 with
# five (21 igieL) and Russian counts it with one (21 igla), so the two files
# cannot share a header.
#
# To bring this file up to date after the English has moved:
#     python scripts/dev/gen_pot.py --merge ru
msgid ""
msgstr ""
"Project-Id-Version: Find The Needle\n"
"Language: ru\n"
"MIME-Version: 1.0\n"
"Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8\n"
"Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit\n"
"Plural-Forms: nplurals=3; plural=(n%10==1 && n%100!=11 ? 0 : n%10>=2 && n%10<=4 && (n%100<10 || n%100>=20) ? 1 : 2);\n"

msgid "SMALL"
msgstr "МАЛАЯ"

msgid "Designed for weaker computers. A shorter hunt with room to walk around the pile."
msgstr "Для слабых компьютеров. Охота покороче, и вокруг кучи есть где пройти."

msgid "STANDARD"
msgstr "СТАНДАРТ"

msgid "The yard as it comes. The pile the game was built around, under one steel roof."
msgstr "Двор как он есть. Та самая куча, вокруг которой построена игра, под одной стальной крышей."

msgid "BIG"
msgstr "БОЛЬШАЯ"

